\mathbf{E} = \{E_1, E_2, E_3\};\)\\
\mathbf{K} = \{\cos\theta, \sin\phi\},\\)
we find the projection onto \(\mathbf{S}:\)
\[
\mathbf{K} \cdot \mathbf{E} = KE_1 \cos\theta + KE_2 \sin\phi = K(|E_1 \cos\theta + E_2 \sin\phi).\]
Substituting into original expression yields:
\[
KE_1 \cos\theta + KE_2 \sin\phi + \left(\frac{v^2}{\varepsilon_1}-1\right)E_1 = 0;
